==================================================
PHASE 17 — MULTIPLE CORRECT
==================================================

Only start after the base flow is stable.

For multipleCorrect:

- allow multiple options to be selected
- clicking an option toggles it
- maintain selectedOptionIds as a Set

Correct only when:

selectedOptionIds == all option IDs where isCorrect == true

Examples:

Correct:
{A, C}
Correct set:
{A, C}

Incorrect:
{A}

Incorrect:
{A, C, D}

After checking:

- show clear checked states
- distinguish correct and incorrect selections
- reveal correct options when necessary

Reuse the same architecture and visual language.

==================================================
PHASE 18 — NUMERICAL
==================================================

Only start after the base flow is stable.

For numerical questions:

Replace option cards with a numeric input.

Accept:

- integers
- decimals
- positive values
- negative values
- signed values

If numericalLowerLimit and numericalUpperLimit exist:

value >= lower &&
value <= upper

The range is inclusive.

If limits do not exist:

compare safely against correctValue.

correctValue may be a JSON number or string.

Preserve:

- entered value
- checked state
- navigation state

Invalid input must not crash.

